
---

🔵 1. Customer Ledger (Transactions: Invoices, Payments)

A. Sales History (Invoices & Sales)

Back Office → Sales → Sales History → Export

You will get:

Sale ID

Date

Customer

Products

Quantities

Totals

Payments breakdown

Sale type (sale / return / on-account)


This is the closest to “invoice header + lines”.

B. On-Account Balances (Customer ledger-like)

Back Office → Customers → Export Customers

Exports:

Customer details

On-Account balance


But does NOT include line-by-line ledger history.
You need to reconstruct ledger using:

Sales History (on-account sales)

Payments Report (on-account payments)


C. Payments Report (Payments ledger)

Back Office → Reporting → Payments → Export

Gives:

Payment date

Payment method

Amount

Customer

Sale ID


This plus Sales History = Full customer ledger.


---

🔵 2. Sales Orders (Quotes / On-hold sales)

Sales Orders (Held sales)

Back Office → Sales → Parked Sales → Export

Gives:

Sales order header

Customer

Line items

Totals



---

🔵 3. Sales Invoices (Header & Lines)

Lightspeed X-Series does not have a separate “invoice module” UI, but an invoice = a completed sale.

So use:

Sales → Sales History → Export


This includes both header + line-level detail.


---

🔵 4. Purchase Orders (Header & Lines)

Stock Orders

Back Office → Inventory → Stock Control → Stock Orders → Export

Exports:

PO header (Supplier, Order #, Dates)

PO line items

Quantities ordered/received

Costs

Outlet (location)



---

🔵 5. Purchase Invoices (Header & Lines)

In X-Series:

A “Purchase Invoice” is created automatically when a Stock Order is marked Received.


They appear in: Inventory → Stock Control → Stock Orders → Export

The export includes:

Received quantities

Received cost value

Supplier invoice number (if entered)


This serves as the "purchase invoice".


---

🔵 6. Items (Products)

Product List

Back Office → Inventory → Products → Export

Exports:

Product ID

Description

SKU

Supplier

Brand

Cost / price

Stock on hand (by outlet)



---

🔵 7. Item Ledger Entry (Stock Tracking)

Lightspeed does not have an “Item Ledger Entry” like an ERP.

But you can extract the stock movement components:

A. Stock order receipts

Inventory → Stock Control → Stock Orders → Export

B. Stock takes (counts)

Inventory → Stock Control → Stock Counts → Export

C. Stock transfers

Inventory → Stock Control → Transfers → Export

D. Sales History (for stock deductions)

Sales → Sales History → Export

With these four you can rebuild the item ledger manually.


---

🔵 8. Vendors (Suppliers)

Supplier List

Back Office → Inventory → Suppliers → Export

Exports:

Supplier name

Contact info

Default costs

Supplier codes



---

🔵 9. Vendor Ledger Entry

Lightspeed X-Series does not track supplier payments.

Therefore:

No “vendor ledger”

No accounts payable

No supplier balances


You can only export Purchase Orders (i.e., stock orders) as above.


---

🔵 10. Payment Terms

There is no Payment Terms module in X-Series.

You can only extract:

(Optional) Custom text fields inside product or customer exports

Nothing structured like “30 days EOM”



---

🔵 11. Locations

Outlet List

Back Office → Setup → Outlets → Export

Exports:

Outlet names

Addresses

Registers



---

🔵 12. Currency

Lightspeed X-Series is single-currency per account.

There is:

No currency export

No exchange rate table

No multicurrency ledger


Currency is the account-level default.


---

🔵 13. Fixed Assets (Hiring Equipment)

Lightspeed has no fixed asset module.

If your hire equipment is entered as products, you can extract:

Inventory → Products → Export


But there is no depreciation or asset tracking.


---

🔵 14. Manufacturers / Brands

Brand List

Back Office → Inventory → Brands → Export

Exports:

Brand ID

Brand name
